# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Cursor Rules

> **Sync note**: The "Key rules" section below summarises `docs/agents/CONVENTIONS.md`. If you update that file, update the summary here too. Agent config files in this repo: {{AGENT_CONFIG_FILES_LIST}}.

Read these files before starting any work in this repository:

1. **`docs/agents/OVERVIEW.md`** — project context, architecture, tech stack, build commands.
2. **`docs/agents/CONVENTIONS.md`** — all hard constraints and contribution rules. Non-negotiable.
3. **`docs/agents/STATUS.md`** — current status and priority backlog.

---

## Key rules

- **Plan before you code**: Write out every file you will create/modify and why, state what you will NOT do, and wait for explicit human approval before writing implementation code. Silence is not approval.
- **`{{CHECK_COMMAND}}` must pass** before every commit.
- **TDD is mandatory**: write tests before or alongside logic changes, in the same commit.
- **Read before you edit**: read a file before your first edit to it in a session (re-read if it may have changed since), and grep for every call site before changing a function signature or public API.
- **Docs are part of done**: update `docs/agents/STATUS.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/issues.md`, and `docs/dev-setup.md` (if deps/tools changed) in the same commit.
- **Commit via `scripts/agent-commit.sh`**: it adds the agent trailer (`{{COAUTHOR_LINE}}`) so the post-commit hook logs the commit as agent-authored.
- **Merge policy**: `{{MERGE_POLICY}}`. Before any push/merge, review every `manual` commit in the range (`docs/commit-log.md` lists them).
- **Hygiene**: keep `README.md`, `.gitignore`, `CODEOWNERS`, and IDE configs current — see `CONTRIBUTING.md §12`.

